WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:16.164
Mr. Smith: Who can tell me what papier-mâché can be used for?

2
00:00:16.165 --> 00:00:21.588
Danny: "For." Four? At four o'clock, we get to go home.

3
00:00:21.589 --> 00:00:25.717
Mr. Smith: Danny! If you have something to say, please raise your hand first.

4
00:00:25.718 --> 00:00:31.209
Chuck: Yeah! Stop interrupting!

5
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.386
Mr. Smith: Settle down everyone.

6
00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:39.280
Mr. Smith: Now, Danny, if you are not going to contribute to the class, [n3@please keep your thoughts to yourself.

7
00:00:39.281 --> 00:00:46.171
Danny: Yes, Mr. Smith.

8
00:00:46.172 --> 00:00:49.000
Mr. Smith: Danny! I told you to settle down.

9
00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:51.707
Danny: Sorry, my face was itchy!

10
00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:54.523
Mr. Smith: Now, this is your homework for the summer.

11
00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:58.046
Mr. Smith: I want you to make a papier-mâché sculpture.

12
00:00:58.047 --> 00:01:00.951
Mr. Smith: It should illustrate something from your life.

13
00:01:00.952 --> 00:01:05.335
Mr. Smith: It must be done when you come back to class in the fall.

14
00:01:05.336 --> 00:01:06.770
Mr. Smith: Yes, Danny?

15
00:01:06.771 --> 00:01:09.665
Danny: Can we make anything for our project?

16
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:12.780
Mr. Smith: Yes, as long as it's from your life.

17
00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:16.887
Danny: So we could make miniatures?

18
00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:22.038
Mr. Smith: Yes, but I don't see what's so funny about it. Yes, Tina?

19
00:01:22.039 --> 00:01:26.356
Tina: Can we do something giant?

20
00:01:26.357 --> 00:01:32.629
Mr. Smith: Well, it would take a lot of work, but you could if you wanted.

21
00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:38.983
Mr. Smith: All right, everyone. Have a good summer!

22
00:01:38.984 --> 00:01:40.100
Mr. Smith: Danny!

23
00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:42.063
Danny: What?

24
00:01:42.064 --> 00:01:44.831
Mr. Smith: Try not to get into too much trouble, okay?

25
00:01:44.832 --> 00:01:47.060
Danny: I'll try, Mr. Smith.

26
00:01:47.061 --> 00:01:48.636
Mr. Smith: Have a nice summer.

27
00:01:48.637 --> 00:01:53.523
Brad: We will. Have a nice summer, Mr. Smith.

28
00:01:53.524 --> 00:01:57.591
Mr. Smith: Do you have the spit balls?

29
00:01:57.592 --> 00:01:59.972
Danny: Do you have the straws?

30
00:01:59.973 --> 00:02:06.579
Brad: Perfect.

31
00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:10.246
Brad: Shh. Surprise is the key.

32
00:02:10.247 --> 00:02:12.401
Danny: Are you ready to run?

33
00:02:12.402 --> 00:02:16.180
Brad: Remember, we'll run right toward the bushes.

34
00:02:16.181 --> 00:02:18.305
Danny: Got it. Ready?

35
00:02:18.306 --> 00:02:25.915
One, two, three!

36
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.543
Chuck: What the─?

37
00:02:28.544 --> 00:02:32.299
Dave: Do you guys have a death wish?

38
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.543
Chuck: Oh, that's it!

39
00:02:34.544 --> 00:02:43.355
Dave: You'd better run for your lives!

40
00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:46.810
Chuck: Stupid little boys!

41
00:02:46.811 --> 00:02:49.265
Dave: Hurry! Let's get them!

42
00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:52.730
Chuck: Those two are going to have a bad summer!

43
00:02:52.731 --> 00:02:58.972
Dave: Yeah! After we break their bones!
